course: dictionary
lesson: 4835
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and hyacinth is one of them. It can name a flower, a colour, a character in a Greek story, or a plant that floats on a lake. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Read «The biggest are the macaws of Central and South American forests; a hyacinth macaw is about a metre long.» Macaw is a clue. Macaws are parrots, so here hyacinth names a bird, not a flower. Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence tell me?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Swap «a hyacinth» for «a flower» and see if it still makes sense. A hyacinth in a glass of water on the windowsill makes sense as a flower, but a hyacinth that cracks palm nuts does not.
fact: A hyacinth is a spring plant that grows from a bulb and has a spike of small, sweet-smelling, bell-shaped flowers.
fact: Hyacinth can also mean a purplish-blue colour.
fact: In Greek stories, Hyacinthus was a young man loved by the god Apollo, and a flower grew from his blood after he died.
fact: A water hyacinth is a floating plant that can cover rivers and lakes.
fact: «The hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail», and «its beak cracks palm nuts so hard that people need a hammer».
exercise: In a science lesson, what is a hyacinth? | A type of fish | A large metal tool | *A spring plant grown from a bulb | A kind of cloud
exercise: «The hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.» What kind of animal is a hyacinth macaw? | *A parrot | A flower | A tree | A fish
exercise: Jayden reads about a water hyacinth covering a lake. What is a water hyacinth? | A bulb with a spike of bells | A bird that sings on the water | *A floating plant that can cover rivers and lakes | A purple cloth
test: In the Greek story, what grew from the blood of Hyacinthus? | A stone | A river | *A flower | A bird
test: What colour is hyacinth when it means a colour? | Bright yellow | Pure white | Deep black | *Purplish-blue
exam: Ella reads «The hyacinth macaw cracks palm nuts» and says hyacinth must mean a flower. What is the best answer? | *Ella is wrong, because the clue macaw shows hyacinth names a bird | Ella is right, because hyacinth always means a flower | Both meanings fit, so the sentence cannot tell us | The sentence is about a colour
